{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And of Yosef he said: Blessed of YHWH be his land.</b> This blessing is literally drawn from the wellspring of the blessing of Ya'akov, who blessed him with an abundance of produce, because he sustained and provided for all the house of Israel. And here he adds מִמֶּגֶד תְּבוּאֹת שֶׁמֶשׁ וְיָרֵחַ, for they had already bowed to him in his dream, ״וְהִנֵּה הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ וְהַיָּרֵחַ״ etc. (Genesis 37:9)." "<b>And from the head of the ancient mountains, and from the precious things of the everlasting hills.</b> As for why he did not mention the expression ״מֶגֶד״ with regard to הַרְרֵי קֶדֶם, we may say that he hinted that all the merit of the fathers and the mothers would belong to the head of Yosef. For Avraham and Sarah begot only Yitzchak, and Yitzchak — even though he fathered Esav and Ya'akov, in any case ״כִּי בְיִצְחָק יִקָּרֵא לְךָ זָרַע״ (Genesis 21:12) — through some of Yitzchak's seed and not through all his seed; if so, Ya'akov is the principal of his progeny. And concerning Ya'akov it is written (Genesis 37:2): ״אֵלֶּה תּוֹלְדוֹת יַעֲקֹב יוֹסֵף״ — if so, Yosef is the principal of all progeny. Therefore all the merit of the fathers and the mothers, which are established in mountains and hills — everything belongs to Yosef. This is what it says: ״וּמֵרֹאשׁ הַרְרֵי קֶדֶם״, for the fathers preceded the world and their merit will stand for him to gore all the ends of the earth — for war belongs to the men and not to the women, but the women are disposed toward producing the fruit of the womb; therefore their merit will stand for him so that his land be filled with precious things. And this is what it says: ״וּמִמֶּגֶד גִּבְעוֹת עוֹלָם״. And this is why he explained these two kinds of blessing in saying ״בְּכוֹר שׁוֹרוֹ הָדָר לוֹ״, for this concerns the abundance of produce, through the merit of the mothers — גִּבְעוֹת עוֹלָם — as ״רָב תְּבוּאוֹת בְּכֹחַ שׁוֹר״ (Proverbs 14:4). ״וְקַרְנֵי רְאֵם קַרְנָיו״ — this concerns victory in war, through the merit of רֹאשׁ הַרְרֵי קֶדֶם." "<b>And they are the myriads of Efrayim.</b> For his name is based on ״כִּי הִפְרַנִי אֱלֹהִים״ (Genesis 41:52), and the myriads were given to him from the blessing of Ya'akov. And his name indicates both the abundance of fruit and the abundance of those who issue from his thigh, which is not so with Menasheh; therefore it says: ״וְהֵם אַלְפֵי מְנַשֶּׁה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:42.339526461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}